@startuml
title UTrabajo — Límites de confianza S13
left to right direction

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam packageBorderColor #667085
skinparam packageFontColor #101828
skinparam packageFontStyle bold

package "Zona cliente · red no confiable" as ClientZone #FFF4E5 {
  actor "Usuario" as User
  node "Dispositivo\nAndroid" as Android
  User --> Android : interacción
}

package "Zona de aplicación" as AppZone #EAF2FF {
  node "API Spring Boot" as API {
    component "Spring Security" as Sec
    component "Controllers" as Ctrl
    component "Services / Auth" as Svc

    Sec --> Ctrl : principal autenticado
    Ctrl --> Svc : caso de uso
  }

  component "Endpoints internos\nexperimentales" as Internal
}

package "Zona de datos privados" as DataZone #ECFDF3 {
  database "PostgreSQL 16" as DB
  folder "Upload storage" as Files
}

cloud "Zona de supply chain\nCI / dependencias / imágenes" as Supply #F4F3FF

Android --> Sec : TB-1 · HTTPS/JSON + Bearer\n(HTTP solo en entorno local)
Svc --> DB : TB-2 · JDBC parametrizado
Svc --> Files : TB-3 · lectura / escritura
Files -[#C2410C]-> Android : TB-4 · riesgo actual: /uploads/** público
Supply --> API : TB-5 · build / runtime
Internal --> Sec : TB-6 · X-Integration-Token

note bottom of ClientZone
Fuera del entorno local,
HTTPS es obligatorio.
end note

note bottom of DataZone
Control objetivo: documentos sensibles
mediante descarga autenticada o URL firmada.
end note

note bottom of Supply
Revisar Actions, dependencias e imágenes;
Git/CI no eliminan el riesgo de supply chain.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Límite |= Cruce de confianza |
  | TB-1 | cliente / red → autenticación de API |
  | TB-2 | servicio → PostgreSQL |
  | TB-3 | servicio → almacenamiento de archivos |
  | TB-4 | archivos públicos → cliente |
  | TB-5 | supply chain → build / runtime |
  | TB-6 | endpoint interno → autenticación de API |
endlegend
@enduml
